SOP: Disable Direct SSH Root Login on All App Servers

Section                              Details
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Objective        Disable direct SSH root login across all app servers in the Stratos Datacenter for improved security.

Pre-Requisites   SSH access to each app server (stapp01, stapp02, stapp03), sudo or root privileges.

Step 1           SSH into each app server:
                 • ssh tony@172.16.238.10 (stapp01)
                 • ssh steve@172.16.238.11 (stapp02)
                 • ssh banner@172.16.238.12 (stapp03)

Step 2           Switch to the root user:
                 sudo su -

Step 3           Navigate to the SSH configuration directory:
                 cd /etc/ssh

Step 4           Open the SSH daemon configuration file:
                 vi sshd_config

Step 5           Locate the line containing:
                 #PermitRootLogin yes
                 or
                 PermitRootLogin yes

Step 6           Modify it as follows:
                 PermitRootLogin no

Step 7           Save and exit the file:
                 :wq

Step 8           Restart the SSH service to apply changes:
                 systemctl restart sshd

Step 9           Verify SSH service is active:
                 systemctl status sshd

Step 10          Test SSH root login (should be denied):
                 ssh root@<server_ip>
                 Expected: Permission denied

Expected Result  Root SSH login is disabled on all app servers. Only non-root users
                 with sudo privileges can SSH into servers.

Rollback Plan    Edit /etc/ssh/sshd_config again and revert:
                 PermitRootLogin yes
                 Then restart SSH:
                 systemctl restart sshd

End State        All app servers deny direct SSH login to root users, enforcing
                 best security practices.
